# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now encode the same data vector $\\vec{x} = "
"\\left(\\textstyle\\frac{1}{2}\\pi, \\textstyle\\frac{1}{3}\\pi\\right)$ to "
"a ZFM circuit with three repetitions, $r=3$, using the Qiskit "
"[`z_feature_map`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ZFeatureMap)"
" class, which altogether gives us the quantum feature map "
"$\\mathscr{U}_{\\text{ZFM}}(\\vec{x})$. By default in the `z_feature_map` "
"class, parameters $\\beta$ are multiplied by 2 before mapping to the phase "
"gate $\\beta \\rightarrow P(\\theta = 2\\beta)$. To reproduce the same "
"encodings as above, we divide by 2.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora codificamos el mismo vector de datos $\\vec{x} = "
"\\left(\\textstyle\\frac{1}{2}\\pi, \\textstyle\\frac{1}{3}\\pi\\right)$ en "
"un circuito ZFM con tres repeticiones, $r=3$, usando la clase "
"[`z_feature_map`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ZFeatureMap)"
" de Qiskit, lo que en conjunto nos da el mapa de características cuántico "
"$\\mathscr{U}_{\\text{ZFM}}(\\vec{x})$. De forma predeterminada en la clase "
"`z_feature_map`, los parámetros $\\beta$ se multiplican por 2 antes de "
"mapearse a la compuerta de fase $\\beta \\rightarrow P(\\theta = 2\\beta)$. "
"Para reproducir las mismas codificaciones que arriba, dividimos por 2.\n"

